# CODEOWNERS — required reviewers by code area
# Syntax: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# This is the ONE place in the repository where personal GitHub handles are used:
# GitHub's enforcement configuration requires literal accounts/teams here, so
# role-based wording is not possible. Everywhere else, policy prose uses roles
# (see CLAUDE.md §2, "Company source precedence").
#
# Every rule below names TWO qualified reviewers with write access, so review of
# a protected path never depends solely on the author or the latest pusher:
# whichever of them authored the change, the other can satisfy the requirement.
# GitHub requires an approval from ANY ONE of the owners listed on the matching
# rule, and the last matching rule wins.
#
# NOTE: an owner must have write access to be valid. These handles were verified
# against the current repository collaborator list. Confirm the current people
# against the live Org Chart before changing this file.
#
# TODO on company-org migration (docs/github-org-migration-plan.md): replace
# these individual handles with GitHub teams (e.g. @<org>/theme-reviewers,
# @<org>/governance-owners) so membership is managed by the company rather than
# by editing this file.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Default: everything in the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                                   @izzaahmed02 @yusra1002

